      "id": 192153,
      "name": "cajunjoel",
      "username": "cajunjoel1",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/d6d6ee/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-03-18T20:11:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Okay, it looks like I need better monitoring than \"server alive\".</p><p>One of the servers that runs the site was down(-ish) and not responding to web requests, but was still receiving traffic and if you hit the bad machine (50/50 chance) you got stuck there. It should all be back to normal now. I'm going to keep an eye on things the rest of today and enable more and better monitoring.&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks for your patience. I didn't initially see anything wrong, but I also didn't look as deeply as I could. The intermittent nature of these things is also misleading sometimes. It took a warning of a failed backup to make me look deeper.</p><p>--J</p>",
      "post_number": 14,
